From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:59:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] ppu_lifter: --func-names names functions from a file,
 dispatch stays by address

A second build of the same program from another EBOOT (Killzone HD's EU edition: the same source linked again, its
code moved by up to 0xE8 bytes) lifts every function under a new func_ADDR name, so the integration code that calls
lifted functions by name (the port's native overrides, PPU_LIFT_NATIVE, direct calls) no longer links.

--func-names FILE takes 'ADDR NAME' lines: the function at ADDR is emitted as NAME everywhere the lifter writes its
name (its definition, calls, tail calls, jump-table arms, the header's externals and function_table's name), while
function_table keeps the real address, so dispatch is unchanged. Names must be C identifiers, each given to one
address; a lift where two addresses (functions or the externals it declares) would end up with one name stops with
a message. Without the option the output
is what it was. tools/test_ppu_func_names.py checks the names, the address in function_table, that only the names
differ from a plain lift, and the two refusals.
---
 tools/ppu_lifter.py          | 79 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 tools/test_ppu_func_names.py | 53 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 121 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tools/test_ppu_func_names.py

